There's a very easy way to fix it:
1) Make absolutely sure that nobody on the computer is playing NetHack
right now. (This should be easy, because you're likely to be the only
person using your own computer.)
2) Delete the file record_lock in the NetHack playfield directory. (If
it isn't there, try looking for a lock directory, and deleting a file
named "record_lock" there.)

Incidentally, the error occurs in the first place if NetHack is forced
to quit while it's writing out the high-score table; it's happened to
me when I've been testing TAEB, and something's gone wrong with the
way it runs NetHack. It might be worth looking at the file "record"
itself and deleting any incomplete lines at the end, in addition to
getting rid of the lockfile, but every time I've seen the error happen
in the wild, there's been nothing wrong with record itself, just a
stray lockfile.

